  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "Given, $\\quad f(x)=5 x-3$ and $g(x)=x^2+3$\nLet, $y=f(x), \\therefore y=5 x-3$\n$y+3=5 x \\Rightarrow x=\\frac{y+3}{5}$\n$\\therefore \\quad f^{-1}(y)=\\frac{y+3}{5} \\Rightarrow f^{-1}(x)=\\frac{x+3}{5}$\nNow, $\\quad g(x)=x^2+3$\nSo, $g \\circ f^{-1}(3)=g\\left[f^{-1}(3)\\right]$\n$=g\\left(\\frac{3+3}{5}\\right)=g\\left(\\frac{6}{5}\\right)=\\frac{(6)^2}{(5)^2}+3=\\frac{36}{25}+3=\\frac{111}{25}$",
    "image": null
  },
